<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keladi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keladi is a village in the Shimoga district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malnad">Malnad</a> hills near Sagar. It was the original seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keladi-nayakas">Keladi Nayakas</a>, local chiefs who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> from about 1499 and later ruled the region independently from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikkeri">Ikkeri</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bednur">Bidanur</a>. Its Rameshwara temple dates from their rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keladi.jpg" alt="Keladi" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dineshkannambadi (talk) 16:39, 26 May 2008 (UTC) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rameshwara_Temple_in_Keladi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
